{"title":"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the interior of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88bdfa5130db58397b818ef56123b898abcbe7a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1P_2P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Point\" title=\"Point\">point</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is given.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/841ee6f0a6ce21be0579ae188e9770097a7e992d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1,Q_2,Q_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Intersection\" title=\"Intersection\">intersections</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fed8008407b90a39b175482d157ba7d4c7fdb4a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PP_1, PP_2,PP_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" /> with the opposing <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Edge\" title=\"Edge\">edges</a> of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88bdfa5130db58397b818ef56123b898abcbe7a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1P_2P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />.  Prove that among the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ratio\" title=\"Ratio\">ratios</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/480559d29abfd15ed5cf3142a905a7df67bf2e8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{PP_1}{PQ_1},\\frac{PP_2}{PQ_2},\\frac{PP_3}{PQ_3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"134\" height=\"41\" /> there exists one not larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and one not smaller than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3SQKgeFlMiA?si=5vhw28fTN2L4qRqr\">https://youtu.be/3SQKgeFlMiA?si=5vhw28fTN2L4qRqr</a> [Video Solution by little-fermat]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/3/d33cc80fa8f093e155c5be46d2e5d9da3d7e1ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> denote the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88bdfa5130db58397b818ef56123b898abcbe7a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1P_2P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25bea95f654f24075c491de3fc8b20aa87b0556.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PP_2P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> share the base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/3/a9348a9dad685bdbb3d87af488461736640f0505.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/b/f8b5d429339a3451b1623d8a3a5e15cc8e1ca3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[PP_2P_3]}{[P_1P_2P_3]}=\\frac{PQ_1}{P_1Q_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"138\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae360f935a7d6cfbcf6c615ebe6421d5e839f4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[PP_1P_3]}{[P_1P_2P_3]}=\\frac{PQ_2}{P_2Q_2}, \\frac{[PP_1P_2]}{[P_1P_2P_3]}=\\frac{PQ_3}{P_3Q_3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"287\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Adding all of these gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/9/20957e9934374f7f98d62319f45b23eb7ad1f122.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[PP_1P_3]}{[P_1P_2P_3]}+\\frac{[PP_1P_2]}{[P_1P_2P_3]}+\\frac{[PP_2P_3]}{[P_1P_2P_3]}=\\frac{PQ_2}{P_2Q_2}+\\frac{PQ_3}{P_3Q_3}+\\frac{PQ_1}{P_1Q_1}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"494\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>We see that we must have at least one of the three fractions not greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, and at least one not less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. These correspond to ratios <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1de4a7d1d42058269997708f661c54317eb2418e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{PP_i}{PQ_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"36\" height=\"41\" /> being less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, so we are done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/1/221146b5c54201e132bf8a8338d7d5798a1faba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K_1=[P_2PP_3], K_2=[P_3PP_1],$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"231\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8acc712c288ce3241ee2371cf2c29c12b7fff0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K_3=[P_1PP_2].$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" />  Note that by same base in triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a6457ef769c3c3e7e0063947657223854b8cd484.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2PP_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/b/90b325f1bf009102e06984404ca9a12b8262ce52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2P_1P_3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/3/713f8705f9af55be3d9bc93296f9934b49344d5e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{P_1P}{PQ_1}+1=\\frac{P_1Q_1}{PQ_1}=\\frac{[P_2P_1P_3]}{[P_2PP_3]}=\\frac{K_1+K_2+K_3}{K_1}.\\]\" width=\"379\" height=\"43\" />  Thus,    <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/645cd0730d119172409f2a3963b0cea70056d2dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{P_1P}{PQ_1}=\\frac{K_2+K_3}{K_1}\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"40\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/0/1203cfaa4bbd00ac361f28a26de73103056cbd80.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{P_2P}{PQ_2}=\\frac{K_1+K_3}{K_2}\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"40\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/d/41db9d05c2e4da6f7e2a1682c292383d8f0460b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{P_3P}{PQ_3}=\\frac{K_1+K_2}{K_3}.\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"40\" />\nWithout loss of generality, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bf8409b500238a849ae856a07ce19af6975c25a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K_1\\leq K_2\\leq K_3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"15\" /> Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/6/f264380d49bbb5524b9fe345de7174eb4e88daa7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{P_1P}{PQ_1}=\\frac{K_2+K_3}{K_1}\\geq \\frac{K_1+K_1}{K_1}=2\\]\" width=\"263\" height=\"40\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/47019be75e031ec72dffd5f62be287100f5949b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{P_3P}{PQ_3}=\\frac{K_1+K_2}{K+3}\\leq \\frac{K_3+K_3}{K_3}=2,\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"40\" /> as desired. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO\" title=\"1961 IMO\">1961 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016194612\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 184/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6407/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.639      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.639      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4852:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016194612 and revision id 197819. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}